  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E97D68">Definition <span data-tag="E97D68">5.4.2.1</span>.</a>accessible!$\infty $-category$\kappa $-accessible $\infty $-category$\infty $-category!accessible Let $\kappa $ be a regular cardinal. An $\infty $-category $\calC $ is <em>$\kappa $-accessible</em> if there exists a small $\infty $-category $\calC ^{0}$ and an equivalence $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calC ^{0}) \rightarrow \calC $. We will say that $\calC $ is <em>accessible</em> if it is $\kappa $-accessible for <em>some</em> regular cardinal $\kappa $. </p>
